s still involved.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Lists MikeWang by commit count and does not credit Mei Chen with Time7. It names Mei Chen and Ravi Menon as recent maintainers.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Credits only Ravi Menon as the author in the renamed file's history. It lists the original authors but gives no share and no Overfelt dominance.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It treats Alex Rowe as probably one person but unconfirmed, and it calls Noor Haddad, Mei Chen and Sam Okafor quiet.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Treats Kofi's 1970 date as a bad timestamp but does not call him active. It lists Sam Okafor as a recent maintainer of time.go.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Names Paul Borman main author of time.go with 73.0% of lines including blanks. It says he left the project. Its dates differ: last commit anywhere is given as 2016, where the truth is 2023. The key point, a main author who is gone, holds.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Names MikeWang as main author of version7.go with 81.2%. It credits Mei Chen with the Time7 accessor at 9.4% and says Ravi Menon only committed it.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Follows the SQL files and names Justin Overfelt as the largest author. His share is 39.6% on database_sql.go alone, inside the range, although the combined figure is 57%. It lists Stone, Wheeler and Souza and says all are gone. Ravi Menon is not credited as author.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Says only 4 of 52 people are active and they hold 4.3% of the lines, so departed people hold about 95.7%. It does not name Ravi, Alex and Kofi as the active set. It treats Alex Rowe as one person and says none of the three files has a meaningful active share, except that it recommends Rowe or Mei Chen. It calls Mei Chen active, which is wrong against the truth. The share of departed owners is right, but the active-people list is wrong.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Says Okafor holds none of time.go's lines. It does not mention Noor Haddad or Kofi Mensah, so it does not cover the noise items fully. It also says no bots or generated files were left out.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"The final answer is only a note about a background task. It contains no analysis.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"No content on version7.go.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"No content on the SQL code.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"No content on who is still active.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"No content on the noise items.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Credits time.go to Sam Okafor at 100% per blame, which the criterion lists as a fail.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Gives MikeWang about 86% and Mei Chen 11 lines for version7.go. It does not say Mei wrote the Time7 accessor, and it tells the reader to check who authored the recent commits.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Uses blame on database_sql.go with Overfelt 26, Stone 11, Wheeler 8 and Souza 8, which matches the truth. It says all are gone and Ravi Menon only did the rename.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Gives no share of lines owned by departed people. It treats Alex Rowe as probably one person, unconfirmed, and it recommends Mei Chen as a reviewer.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Names Sam Okafor as the author of all of time.go, which fails the criterion.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":16151,"type":"result","duration_ms":16173,"uuid":"a1d4aeac-c63e-44c9-8a9d-2642fecd1d1c","ttft_stream_ms":2167,"time_to_request_ms":666,"first_content_frame_ms":2167,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
